          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":477,\"filmId\":372,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-07-05T15:15\",\"doorsTime\":\"2:45pm\",\"filmTime\":\"3:15pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":3,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"isPrivate\":false,\"memberOnly\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":372,\"title\":\"THE ROAD TO SALINA\",\"description\":\"A young drifter traveling through a remote desert road stops at a roadside café and service station run by a woman who mistakes him for her long-lost son, Rocky. He initially plays along, but the situation becomes increasingly unsettling as others around him also treat him as Rocky, raising questions about identity, memory, and deception.\\n\\nAs the situation develops, the story leans into ambiguity and psychological unease, with shifting relationships and unclear histories creating a persistent sense of disorientation. The desert setting and isolated location intensify the feeling of a closed, unstable world where certainty never fully forms.\",\"runtime\":96,\"year\":1970,\"country\":\"France, Italy\",\"director\":\"Georges Lautner\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://images.mubicdn.net/images/film/47031/cache-37496-1745490581/image-w1280.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
