          ],
          "headersSize": 708,
          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":482,\"filmId\":424,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-07-06T18:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"6:00pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6:30pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":20,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"isPrivate\":false,\"memberOnly\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":424,\"title\":\"THE LADY OF THE BLACK MOONS\",\"description\":\"Housewife Aida is trapped in a loveless marriage to the wealthy Samir. Unsatisfied with life and love, she daydreams about her sensual affair with driver Omar and at night goes to Victoria’s, a gothic brothel where her darkest desires are catered to. But every full moon she is overcome by a nightmarish visions, afflicted by a curse that threatens to drive her insane. \\n\\nA class-melodrama wrapped up in arthouse pretensions, softcore erotica and the fantastique – this is a dark gem from early 1970s Lebanese cinema. There are shades of Belle de Jour and Eyes Wide Shut in Egyptian star Nahed Yousri’s depiction of repressed desire, but Lady of the Black Moons feels like nothing else. Directed during a period of loosened censorship in Lebanon, Samir A Khouri’s mystical and sensual sexploitation flick has been called “the crowning achievement of this short-lived wave” (BFI). \\n\\nWe are proud to present this rare screening with all proceeds donated to community centre Beit Aam in Beirut. Introduced by Harry Thorfinn-George. \",\"runtime\":104,\"year\":1971,\"country\":\"Lebanon\",\"director\":\"Samir A. Khouri\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://yxvwcvyczjjes5ua.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/ChatGPT%20Image%20Jun%2017%2C%202026%2C%2012_56_11%20PM.png\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":93,\"ageCertificate\":\"15\"}}",
