            }
          ],
          "headersSize": 708,
          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":501,\"filmId\":413,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-07-15T18:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"6:00pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6:30pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":19,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"isPrivate\":false,\"memberOnly\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":413,\"title\":\"THE SWIMMER\",\"description\":\"On a summer afternoon in suburban Connecticut, Ned Merrill unexpectedly appears at the home of friends and decides to return to his own house by swimming across every pool in the neighbourhood. What begins as a whimsical challenge gradually becomes an odyssey through a landscape of garden parties, tennis courts, and affluent back gardens. As Ned moves from one property to the next, encounters with friends, former lovers, and acquaintances begin to reveal unsettling gaps between his self-image and the reality of his circumstances.\\n\\nAdapted from John Cheever's celebrated short story, The Swimmer transforms the post-war American suburb into a dreamlike psychological landscape. Released at the end of the 1960s, the film uses the apparent prosperity of upper-middle-class America as the backdrop for a meditation on memory, denial, ageing, and personal collapse. Burt Lancaster's performance anchors a work that shifts almost imperceptibly from social satire to existential tragedy, creating one of the most distinctive and enigmatic films of its era. Through its fragmented journey across a seemingly ordinary suburban environment, The Swimmer exposes the anxieties and disillusionments concealed beneath the mythology of American success.\",\"runtime\":95,\"year\":1968,\"country\":\"USA\",\"director\":\"Frank Perry & Sydney Pollack\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://static1.squarespace.com/static/59e512ddf43b55c29c71b996/59ece61c14fd83f0bbe30ee9/6075e0f41b1eca5c4fc968af/1666987551036/the_swimmer_2.jpg?format=1500w\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"12\"}}",
