          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":518,\"filmId\":306,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-07-22T18:00\",\"doorsTime\":\"5:30pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6:00pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":6,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"isPrivate\":false,\"memberOnly\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":306,\"title\":\"FREAK ORLANDO\",\"description\":\"A stylised episodic journey follows Orlando, a figure who moves through a series of grotesque and theatrical tableaux, encountering a parade of eccentric characters, social archetypes, and distorted versions of history and identity. Across these shifting episodes, the boundaries between gender, time, and reality dissolve into a carnival-like procession of spectacle and performance.\\n\\nStructured like a surreal stage play, the film turns its attention to the performative nature of identity, using costume, exaggeration, and absurdist humour to dismantle fixed ideas of gender and normality. Its deliberately artificial style creates a world where transformation is constant and nothing remains stable for long.\\n\\nIntroduced and programmed by Juno Valentine\",\"runtime\":126,\"year\":1981,\"country\":\"West Germany\",\"director\":\"Ulrike Ottinger\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/16046936216262b713e766620921ec27a.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
